From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:47:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Share a rest between two voices of a staff

When two voices of a staff rest together, engravers print one rest; the
rhythm algorithm gives it to one voice only. The other voice's next chord
then got the end of that voice's previous chord as its time, i.e. the time
of the rest, a slot to its left, and when the voices disagreed the lowest
time won: the chord, and the chords of the other voice in its slot, came
a beat early and the voices ended short of the measure.

Now a voice that ends exactly where a rest of another voice on the same
staff starts, in an earlier slot, is free at the end of that rest (and of
consecutive shared rests): MeasureRhythm.voiceEnd is used for the times a
slot infers, for checking a mapping, when applying it, and for extinct
voices. Logged as "after a rest shared with another voice".
